08-0fba095a2ae5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","poiId":"poi-united-kingdom-london-barbican-centre"},{"id":"shoreditch-culture-whitechapel","name":"Whitechapel Gallery","coordinates":[51.5163,-0.0709],"description":"Whitechapel Gallery is the contemporary-art anchor on the Shoreditch edge, useful for a sharper east London culture day beyond street art alone.","hours":{"default":"Check current hours before going."},"photo":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564324144208-0fba095a2ae5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","poiId":"poi-united-kingdom-london-whitechapel-gallery"},{"id":"shoreditch-culture-spitalfields","name":"Old Spitalfields Market","coordinates":[51.5197,-0.0755],"description":"Old Spitalfields Market layers food, fashion, migration history, and East End commerce into a practical stop between Shoreditch and the City.","hours":{"default":"Check current hours before going."},"photo":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1533929736458-ca588d08c8be?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","poiId":"poi-united-kingdom-london-old-spitalfields-market"},{"id":"shoreditch-culture-brick-lane","name":"Brick Lane","coordinates":[51.5217,-0.0717],"description":"Brick Lane is the street-culture corridor for curry houses, markets, murals, vintage shops, and east London identity that should be walked rather than rushed.","hours":{"default":"Check current hours before going."},"photo":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513635269975-59663e0ac1ad?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","poiId":"poi-united-kingdom-london-brick-lane"},{"id":"shoreditch-culture-museum-home","name":"Museum of the Home","coordinates":[51.5314,-0.0765],"description":"Museum of the Home gives Shoreditch a quieter domestic-history stop, with period rooms and gardens that counterbalance the neighborhood''s nightlife image.","hours":{"default":"Check current hours before going."},"photo":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564324144208-0fba095a2ae5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","poiId":"poi-united-kingdom-lon