},{"id":"nature-regents-park","name":"Regent''s Park","coordinates":[51.5313,-0.1569],"description":"Regent''s Park brings formal gardens, open fields, London Zoo, and Primrose Hill access into one of the city''s most useful slow-day routes.","hours":{"default":"Check current hours before going."},"photo":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500462918059-b1a0cb512f1d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","poiId":"poi-united-kingdom-london-regent-s-park"},{"id":"nature-hampstead-heath","name":"Hampstead Heath","coordinates":[51.5608,-0.1657],"description":"Hampstead Heath is the wilder London park day, with ponds, hills, woods, and Parliament Hill views that make the city feel suddenly spacious.","hours":{"default":"Check current hours before going."},"photo":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500462918059-b1a0cb512f1d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","poiId":"poi-united-kingdom-london-hampstead-heath"},{"id":"nature-richmond-park","name":"Richmond Park","coordinates":[51.4479,-0.2743],"description":"Richmond Park is the big western escape, best for deer, long walks, cycling, and a half-day plan that leaves central London behind.","hours":{"default":"Check current hours before going."},"photo":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500462918059-b1a0cb512f1d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","poiId":"poi-united-kingdom-london-richmond-park"},{"id":"nature-greenwich-park","name":"Greenwich Park","coordinates":[51.4769,-0.0005],"description":"Greenwich Park combines views, maritime history, the observatory, and village pacing, making it more than a simple park stop.","hours":{"default":"Check current hours before going."},"photo":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500462918059-b1a0cb512f1d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","poiId":"poi-united-kingdom-london-greenwich-park"},{"id":"nature-regents-canal","name":"Regent''s Canal","coordinates":[51.5396,-0.1454],"description":"Regent''s Canal is the linear London walk for Camden, King''s Cross, Islington, and east London, useful